Dynamic routing in Next.js is achieved through the use of bracket notation in the file names of pages and components. This allows for a flexible and dynamic URL structure, where any route that matches a specific path component or URL path will be handled by that page or component.

For example, suppose you are building a web application with Next.js, and you want to create a post page and a related component named `PostCard`, which displays the post title and author information in an interactive card layout.

To set up dynamic routing for this scenario, you would first need to create two pages: `PostPage` and `PostCard`. Here's how these pages would be structured:

1. `PostPage`: This page would serve as the entry point for navigating to other posts on the site. The page would have a `header` component that would display the site's title, logo, and navigation menu.

Here's an example of what the `Header` component in the `PostPage` could look like:

```jsx
<header>
  <a href="/posts/first-post/">First Post</a>
  <nav class="top-nav">
    <a href="/">Home</a>
    <a href="/about">About Us</a>
    <a href="/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a>
    <a href="/contact-us">Contact Us</a>
  </nav>
</header>
```

1. `PostCard`: This component would serve as the entry point for navigating to other post cards on the site. The component would have a `card` component that would display the post card's title, author information, image file URL, and related links.

Here's an example of what the `Card` component in the `PostCard` could look like:

```jsx
<template>
  <div class="post-card">
    <h3 class="title">{{ title }}</h3>
    <p class="author">{{ author }}</p>
    <img src="{{ imageURL }}" alt="{{ imageAlt }}">
    <ul class="related-links">
      <li><a href="/posts/{{ relatedPostId }}/">Related Post</a></li>
      <!-- Add more related links if needed -->
    </ul>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'PostCard',
  components: {
    Card: ({ title, author }, imageURL)),

    RelatedLinks: () => ({
      RelatedPost: (relatedPostId) =>
        <a href="/posts/{{ relatedPostId }}/">Related Post</a>,
      OtherLink: () => ({
        ImageLink: (imageURL) =>
          <img src={{ imageURL }} alt={{ imageAlt }}></img>,
        Link: () => ({
          Tag: () => ({
            Title: (title) =>
              <h3 class="tag-title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
          Description: (description) =>
          <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      OtherLink: () => ({
        ImageLink: (imageURL) =>
          <img src={{ imageURL }} alt={{ imageAlt }}></img>,
        Link: () => ({
          Tag: () => ({
            Title: (title) =>
              <h3 class="tag-title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
          Description: (description) =>
          <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      ImageLink: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      TagTitle: (title) =>
        <h3 class="tag-title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      LinkTitle: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="link-title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      OtherLinkTitle: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="other-link-title">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      OtherLinkDescription: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="other-link-description">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      OtherLinkTarget: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="other-link-target">{{ title }}</h3>>),
      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>),
      OtherLinkRel: () => ({
        Title: (title) =>
          <h3 class="other-link-rel">{{ title }}</h3>>),

      Description: (description) =>
      <p class="description">{{ description }}</p>>)

};</script>
