    const staticSSGPagesDir = config.moduleOptions.staticDirs.map(dir => `static-ssg-pages/${dir}.js`).join('/')).replace(/\/node_modules\//, '') + '/static-ssg-pages/', {
      exclude: [
        'next-auth.js',
        'assets/js/app.js',
        'components/**'
      ]
    });
  },
};
```

In the above example, we export SSG (Single Page Application) pages to a directory named "static-ssg-pages". The `staticDirs` array in the `configureWebpack` block specifies the directories where SSG pages will be exported.

To deploy your Next.js app, you can use a package like `@nextjs/deployment` or `vercel-deployer`. Here's an example of how to install and configure the `@nextjs/deployment` package on a Node.js server:
```perl
// Install the @nextjs/deployment package
npm install --save-dev @nextjs/deployment

// Create a new Next.js app deployment directory in the `public` folder of your server
NextDeploymentDir = __dirname + '/public';

// Initialize the `@nextjs/deployment` package with an empty configuration file
NextDeploymentInit()

// Configure the `@nextjs/deployment` package to use a custom Next.js app deployment directory
NextDeploymentConfig({
  rootfs: NextDeploymentDir,
})

// Update the `@nextjs/deployment` package configuration file with a new Next.js app deployment directory URL and additional settings for the deployment directory
NextDeploymentInit({
  rootfs: NextDeploymentDir,
  stagingDirURL: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/staging/',
  // Additional settings for the staging directory URL
  // example: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/deployment/''
})

// Verify that the new Next.js app deployment directory URL and additional settings for the staging directory URL are correctly configured in the `@nextjs/deployment` package configuration file
NextDeploymentInit({
  rootfs: NextDeploymentDir,
  stagingDirURL: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/staging/',
  // Additional settings for the staging directory URL
  // example: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/deployment/''
})

// Deploy a new Next.js app deployment directory to your server
NextDeployment()

// Verify that the new Next.js app deployment directory to your server is correctly deployed in the `@nextjs/deployment` package configuration file
NextDeploymentInit({
  rootfs: NextDeploymentDir,
  stagingDirURL: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/staging/',
  // Additional settings for the staging directory URL
  // example: 'https://my-next-js-app.com/deployment/''
})
```

This example demonstrates how to configure a `@nextjs/deployment` package on a Node.js server. The configuration includes setting the rootfs of the deployment directory, specifying the URL of the staging directory in the deployment directory rootfs, and adding additional settings for the deployment directory rootfs. After configuring the `@nextjs/deployment` package, you can deploy a new Next.js app deployment directory to your server using the `NextDeployment()` function.

